Bring your saree and a photo of the design you like: simple cotton blouses for every day, lined silk blouses for functions, and maggam work for weddings.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1610030469983-98e550d6193c?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=2000', array['Princess cut and katori cut', 'Lining and piping in a matching shade', 'Padding and hooks placed for your fit', 'Maggam and aari embroidery on request']::text[], '[{"name":"Princess cut","desc":"Seams run over the bust instead of darts, so the blouse follows your shape closely. Good for silk and brocade."},{"name":"Katori cut","desc":"A cup-shaped panel under the bust gives shape and support without padding. A classic for silk sarees."},{"name":"Back and neck designs","desc":"Deep backs, boat necks, collars and dori ties with tassels. Bring a photo and we will work out what suits the saree."},{"name":"Bridal maggam work","desc":"Hand embroidery with zari, stones and beads, planned with you around the saree border."}]'::jsonb, '[{"title":"Bring the saree to the fitting","desc":"We match the lining, the piping and the sleeve length to the border."},{"title":"Choose the neckline with your jewellery","desc":"A heavy necklace sits best on a round or boat neck. A long chain suits a deeper front."},{"title":"Decide the sleeve length early","desc":"Elbow-length sleeves need more fabric than short ones. Tell us before we cut."}]'::jsonb, 1);

Bridal lehengas, reception and party lehengas, and lighter ones for functions, stitched from your fabric or from a set you have bought.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1595777457583-95e059d581b8?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=2000', array['Kali and umbrella cuts', 'Can-can and lining for volume', 'Waist and length set with your heels on', 'Choli and dupatta finished to match']::text[], '[{"name":"Kalidar","desc":"Made from many tapered panels, so it flares evenly all round. Good for heavy fabric and borders."},{"name":"Umbrella cut","desc":"Cut as a circle for a soft, swinging flare. Good for georgette and chiffon."},{"name":"A-line","desc":"Fitted at the waist and gently flared. Easy to wear through a long function."},{"name":"Bridal","desc":"Heavy fabric, can-can layers and a structured choli, planned around the border and the embroidery."}]'::jsonb, '[{"title":"Wear your heels to the fitting","desc":"We set the hem with the footwear you will wear on the day."},{"title":"Tell us how long you will wear it","desc":"For a long wedding day we keep the waist comfortable and the skirt as light as the fabric allows."},{"title":"Check the fabric length first","desc":"Flared cuts need more fabric. Bring the full set and we will tell you what it allows."}]'::jsonb, 2);

Floor-length gowns for receptions, knee-length anarkalis for festivals, and simpler ones for everyday functions.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1609357605129-26f69add5d6e?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=2000', array['Flare planned for your height', 'Kalidar and umbrella cuts', 'Borders and lace set evenly', 'A can-can layer when you want more volume']::text[], '[{"name":"Floor-length","desc":"A gown-style anarkali that reaches the floor, measured with the heels you will wear."},{"name":"Angrakha","desc":"An overlapping front tied at the side, with or without tassels."},{"name":"Cape style","desc":"A sheer cape over the anarkali in place of a dupatta."}]'::jsonb, '[{"title":"Flow or structure","desc":"Georgette and chiffon fall softly. Silk holds its shape and looks more formal."},{"title":"Measure in your heels","desc":"For a floor-length anarkali we set the length with your footwear on."}]'::jsonb, 3);

Birthday frocks, pattu pavadai for festivals, and lehenga and sharara sets, stitched to your daughter’s measurements.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518831959646-742c3a14ebf7?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=2000', array['Soft lining against the skin', 'No heavy work at the neck or underarms', 'Extra seam margin to let out later', 'Matching outfits for mother and daughter']::text[], '[{"name":"Party frocks","desc":"Net or satin frocks with layers, bows and flowers, lined so they do not scratch."},{"name":"Pattu pavadai","desc":"The traditional silk skirt and blouse for festivals and functions, with the border placed to show."},{"name":"Lehenga and sharara sets","desc":"Light, easy-to-move-in sets for weddings and family functions."}]'::jsonb, '[{"title":"Comfort first","desc":"Keep heavy embroidery away from the neck and underarms, where children feel it most."},{"title":"Leave room to grow","desc":"We keep extra margin in the seams so the dress can be let out as she grows."}]'::jsonb, 4);

